x280: the L2CPU clock table offers 1250, 1350 and 1500 MHz

The PLL4 table held 15, 200, 800, 1000 and 1750 MHz. Three registered solutions are added on the
12.5 MHz reference, mhz = 12.5 * fbdiv / postdiv: 1250 (fbdiv 100), 1350 (108) and 1500 (120), each with
post-dividers 1, 1, 1, 1 as the 800, 1000 and 1750 rows. set_pll steps the divider fields one at a time and
confirms the clock on every L2CPU, as for the other rows.

--- a/tt_metal/fabric/experimental/x280/src/device/x280_pll.cpp
+++ b/tt_metal/fabric/experimental/x280/src/device/x280_pll.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@ constexpr PllSolution kPllSolutions[] = {
     {200, 128, {15, 15, 15, 15}},
     {800, 64, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
     {1000, 80, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
+    {1250, 100, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
+    {1350, 108, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
+    {1500, 120, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
     {1750, 140, {1, 1, 1, 1}},
 };
 
